.el .ds Aq '
.TH garuda-toolbox-packages 1  "garuda-toolbox 6.3.0" 
.SH NAME
garuda\-toolbox\-packages \- Search, show, install and remove the packages of the repositories and the AUR
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgaruda\-toolbox packages\fR [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR \fIWHEN\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR \fICOLUMNS\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Search, show, install and remove the packages of the repositories and the AUR
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print the programs\*(Aq own words under an error
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Print long text directly instead of through `$PAGER`
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Colour the output: auto, always or never
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fI<COLUMNS>\fR
Cut long cells to this many columns
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Leave out the spinner and the hints
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-packages\-search(1)
Search the repository and installed packages by name and description, or the AUR with `\-\-aur`
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-packages\-show(1)
Show one package: where it comes from, its version, size and dependencies, and its files once installed
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-packages\-install(1)
Install packages from the repositories, or build them from the AUR with `\-\-aur`
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-packages\-remove(1)
Remove an installed package with the dependencies nothing else needs
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  garuda\-toolbox packages search editor
  garuda\-toolbox packages install gimp
.SH "SEE ALSO"
garuda\-toolbox(1)
